IMPORT prelude

-- Private Health Insurance Act 2007 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- deciding on hospital cover: Part 2-3 lifetime health cover
-- (s 34-1 the late-joiner increase and "lifetime health cover age"; s 34-5 the increase for dropping cover; s 34-10 the increase
-- stops after 10 years; s 34-15 hospital cover; s 34-20 permitted days without hospital cover; s 34-25 lifetime health cover base
-- day; s 34-30 overseas; ss 37-1, 37-5, 37-7, 37-10, 37-15 and 37-20 exceptions, the 70% cap and joint cover); Part 2-2 the
-- private health insurance rebate as a share of the PHII benefit (ss 22-5, 22-15, 22-20) and the income tiers (ss 22-30, 22-35,
-- 22-40, 22-45); Part 3-2 community rating (ss 55-5, 55-10, 55-15); s 102-1 (an insurer offering general cover must offer
-- hospital cover).
--
-- SEAT: the person deciding on hospital cover -- the adult who asks "When does Lifetime Health Cover loading start, and how much
-- will I pay?", "How much rebate do I get?" and "Can the insurer refuse me or charge me more?". The Act's duties fall on the
-- private health insurer; each is encoded as what it means for that person.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 42, compilation date 19 September 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 90, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00412), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2007A00031.txt. The Private Health Insurance (Lifetime Health
-- Cover) Rules 2015 and the Private Health Insurance (Incentives) Rules are NOT deposited: every matter they settle (suspension
-- days, classes taken to have cover, the rebate adjustment factor) is an INPUT.
--
-- THE DEPOSIT DROPS THE FORMULAS set as images. Section 34-1(2) reads "The amount of the increase is worked out as follows:"
-- and then goes straight to "where:"; s 34-5(2) does the same; so do s 22-40(4) (the increase in the family thresholds for two
-- or more dependent children) and s 22-45(4) (the indexation factor). INFERENCE (not in the deposit): the s 34-1(2) and
-- s 34-5(2) formulas are 2% of the base rate for each year of "lifetime health cover age" over 30, and for each of the "years
-- without hospital cover". The deposit's own words fit that reading: the s 34-1(2) definitions define "base rate" and
-- "lifetime health cover age"; s 34-5(2) defines "base rate" and "years without hospital cover"; and s 37-15 caps "any
-- increase" at 70% of the base rate. The 2% figure is held in one place, `the loading per year, in percent`, so it can be
-- corrected from the authoritative text. The s 22-40(4) increase and the indexed tier thresholds are INPUTS, as in the Medicare
-- Levy Act baseline.
--
-- Dates are numbers written YYYYMMDD (14 March 2003 is 20030314). A first anniversary is the same day a year later (+10000);
-- a 29 February start is not handled.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 34-25(4A), (4B) and s 34-30(1)(a) (Norfolk Island at the final transition time -- `Not covered by this
-- encoding`); s 34-25(2) (a base day on or before 30 June 2010 stands -- answered by saying so, since the old day is not
-- worked out here); s 22-25 (the 65-and-over rate after the older person leaves the policy); s 22-15(5A)-(5E) worked out year
-- by year (the adjusted percentages are INPUTS); Division 23 registration machinery; Division 40 (insurers' notices and
-- records); s 45-1 excess levels (encoded in the Medicare Levy Act baseline); Parts 3-3 and 3-4 beyond s 102-1 (benefit,
-- waiting-period and portability requirements); Chapters 4 to 6 (insurer business, enforcement, the Ombudsman, review);
-- machinery. Borrowed terms are asked as facts: "married" (A New Tax System (Medicare Levy Surcharge -- Fringe Benefits) Act
-- 1999), "child" (ITAA 1997), "income for surcharge purposes" (ITAA 1997), "applicable benefits arrangement" (National Health
-- Act 1953), "gold card" (Veterans' Entitlements and MRCA treatment entitlements), "overseas".
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. Consistent with ../../../medicare-levy-act-1986/encodings/baseline-2026-10, which borrows ss 22-30 to
-- 22-45 and s 45-1 from this Act and uses the same tier names. See NOTES.md.

§ `Private Health Insurance Act 2007 -- hospital cover, the loading, the rebate and community rating`

§§ `Answers and helpers`

DECLARE `Base day answer` IS ONE OF
    `Base day on` HAS `date` IS A NUMBER
    `My base day on or before 30 June 2010 stands`
    `Not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date` MEANS `y` TIMES 10000 PLUS `m` TIMES 100 PLUS `d`

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of` MEANS TRUNC (`d` DIVIDED BY 10000) 0

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month and day of` MEANS `d` MINUS (`the year of` `d` TIMES 10000)

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first anniversary of` MEANS `d` PLUS 10000

-- Whole years of age on day `d` for a person born on `born` (both YYYYMMDD).
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age on` MEANS TRUNC ((`d` MINUS `born`) DIVIDED BY 10000) 0

§§ `s 34-25 -- lifetime health cover base day`

-- s 34-25(1): "a person's lifetime health cover base day is the 1 July after the person turns 31." (Gloss: the day from which
-- not holding hospital cover starts to cost you. A person whose 31st birthday is 1 July waits for the next 1 July.)
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 1 July after turning 31` MEANS
    IF `the month and day of` `born` LESS THAN 701
    THEN `the date` (`the year of` `born` PLUS 31) 7 1
    ELSE `the date` (`the year of` `born` PLUS 32) 7 1

DECLARE `Base day facts` HAS
    `my date of birth` IS A NUMBER
    `I had a lifetime health cover base day on or before 30 June 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was living on Norfolk Island at the final transition time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was an Australian citizen on my medicare eligibility day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my medicare eligibility day` IS A NUMBER
    `I was overseas on the day worked out under s 34-25(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I first returned to or entered Australia after that day, staying 90 days or more` IS A NUMBER

-- s 34-25(3): for a person "who is not an Australian citizen on the person's medicare eligibility day", the base day is "the
-- later of: (a) the 1 July after the person turns 31; and (b) the first anniversary of the person's medicare eligibility day."
-- (Gloss: the medicare eligibility day is the day Services Australia registered you as eligible for Medicare, s 34-25(5).)
GIVEN `f` IS A `Base day facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day under s 34-25(1) or (3)` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `I was an Australian citizen on my medicare eligibility day`
    THEN `the 1 July after turning 31` (`f`'s `my date of birth`)
    ELSE `the greater of` (`the 1 July after turning 31` (`f`'s `my date of birth`))
                          (`the first anniversary of` (`f`'s `my medicare eligibility day`))

-- s 34-25(4): "if the person is overseas on the day worked out under subsection (1) or (3), the person's lifetime health cover
-- base day is the first anniversary of: (a) the person's first return to Australia from overseas; or (b) the person's first entry
-- to Australia; after the day worked out". s 34-30(2): a return or entry for "less than 90 days" does not count.
-- s 34-25(2): a base day "on or before 30 June 2010 ... remains the person's lifetime health cover base day".
@export When is my lifetime health cover base day (s 34-25)?
GIVEN `f` IS A `Base day facts` @desc Your date of birth, citizenship on your Medicare eligibility day, and whether you were overseas on the day
GIVETH A `Base day answer`
DECIDE `When is my base day` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `f`'s `I had a lifetime health cover base day on or before 30 June 2010` THEN `My base day on or before 30 June 2010 stands`
        IF `f`'s `I was living on Norfolk Island at the final transition time` THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
        IF `f`'s `I was overseas on the day worked out under s 34-25(1) or (3)`
           THEN `Base day on` (`the first anniversary of` (`f`'s `the day I first returned to or entered Australia after that day, staying 90 days or more`))
        OTHERWISE `Base day on` (`the day under s 34-25(1) or (3)` `f`)

-- s 37-7: "If the 1 July after a person turns 31 has not arrived, lifetime health cover does not yet apply to the person."
@export Does lifetime health cover apply to me yet (s 37-7)?
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `today` IS A NUMBER @desc Today's date, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does lifetime health cover apply to me yet` IF
    `today` AT LEAST `the 1 July after turning 31` `born`

§§ `s 34-15 -- hospital cover`

-- s 34-15(1): "An adult has hospital cover if he or she is insured under a complying health insurance policy that covers hospital
-- treatment." s 34-15(2): an adult "is taken to have hospital cover" while covered by an applicable benefits arrangement, while
-- holding a gold card, or while in a class specified in the Lifetime Health Cover Rules (not deposited: asked as a fact).
@export Do I have hospital cover for lifetime health cover purposes (s 34-15)?
GIVEN `insured under a complying policy that covers hospital treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are insured under a complying health insurance policy that covers hospital treatment
      `covered by an applicable benefits arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are covered by an applicable benefits arrangement (National Health Act 1953 before 1 April 2007)
      `I hold a gold card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Veterans' or MRCA gold card
      `I am in a class specified in the Lifetime Health Cover Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Lifetime Health Cover Rules treat people like you as having cover
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have hospital cover` IF
       `insured under a complying policy that covers hospital treatment`
    OR `covered by an applicable benefits arrangement`
    OR `I hold a gold card`
    OR `I am in a class specified in the Lifetime Health Cover Rules`

§§ `s 34-1 -- the increase for taking out hospital cover late`

-- INFERENCE: the s 34-1(2) and s 34-5(2) formulas are missing from the deposit (see the header). 2% a year is the figure read
-- here; s 37-15's 70% cap is reached at 35 years.
DECIDE `the loading per year, in percent` IS 2

-- s 34-1(2): "lifetime health cover age, in relation to an adult who takes out hospital cover after his or her lifetime health
-- cover base day, means the adult's age on the 1 July before the day on which the adult took out the hospital cover."
-- (Gloss: if you take out cover on 1 July itself, the 1 July "before" it is the previous year's.)
GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 1 July before` MEANS
    IF `the month and day of` `d` GREATER THAN 701
    THEN `the date` (`the year of` `d`) 7 1
    ELSE `the date` (`the year of` `d` MINUS 1) 7 1

@export What is my lifetime health cover age if I take out hospital cover on a given day (s 34-1(2))?
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `day I take out hospital cover` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you take out hospital cover, YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my lifetime health cover age` IS
    `age on` `born` (`the 1 July before` `day I take out hospital cover`)

-- s 34-1(1): "A private health insurer must increase the amount of premiums payable for hospital cover in respect of an adult
-- if the adult did not have hospital cover on his or her lifetime health cover base day." Exceptions: s 37-1 (born "on or
-- before 1 July 1934"); s 37-5 (31 by 1 July 2000 and overseas that day: "taken ... to have had hospital cover on the person's
-- lifetime health cover base day" -- asked as a fact); s 37-10 (a hardship determination in force before 1 April 2007).
@export Must my hospital cover premiums be increased because I did not have hospital cover on my base day (ss 34-1, 37-1, 37-5, 37-10)?
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `had hospital cover on my base day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had hospital cover on your lifetime health cover base day
      `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 31 and overseas on 1 July 2000 (s 37-5) or had a hardship determination before 1 April 2007 (s 37-10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my premiums be increased for joining late` IF
        (NOT `had hospital cover on my base day`)
    AND (NOT `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover`)
    AND `born` GREATER THAN 19340701

@export By what percentage of the base rate is my premium increased for joining late (s 34-1(2), INFERENCE as to the formula)?
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, YYYYMMDD
      `day I take out hospital cover` IS A NUMBER @desc The day you take out hospital cover, YYYYMMDD
      `had hospital cover on my base day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had hospital cover on your lifetime health cover base day
      `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats you as having had cover
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my late-joiner loading in percent` IS
    IF `Must my premiums be increased for joining late` `born` `had hospital cover on my base day` `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover`
    THEN `the greater of` 0 ((`What is my lifetime health cover age` `born` `day I take out hospital cover` MINUS 30) TIMES `the loading per year, in percent`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 34-5 and 34-20 -- the increase for dropping cover, and permitted days`

-- s 34-20(1): after an adult first ceases to have hospital cover after the base day, the permitted days are "(a) days on which the
-- cover was suspended ... in accordance with the rules for suspensions" (Rules not deposited: the count is an input); "(b) days
-- ... on which the adult is overseas that form part of a continuous period overseas of more than one year"; and "(c) the first
-- 1,094 days (not counting days covered by paragraph (a) or (b)) on which the adult did not have hospital cover." s 34-30(1)(b):
-- a return of less than 90 days is part of the continuous period overseas.
@export How many of my days without hospital cover are not permitted days (s 34-20)?
GIVEN `days without hospital cover since I first dropped it` IS A NUMBER @desc Days after your base day, since you first dropped hospital cover, on which you had none
      `of them, days my cover was suspended under the Rules` IS A NUMBER @desc Days your insurer suspended your cover under the Lifetime Health Cover Rules
      `of them, days overseas in a continuous absence of more than one year` IS A NUMBER @desc Days overseas that were part of a continuous absence of more than a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days without cover count against me` IS
    `the greater of` 0
        (`days without hospital cover since I first dropped it`
         MINUS `of them, days my cover was suspended under the Rules`
         MINUS `of them, days overseas in a continuous absence of more than one year`
         MINUS 1094)

-- s 34-5(2): "years without hospital cover is the number obtained by: (a) dividing by 365 the number of days (other than
-- permitted days without hospital cover) ... on which he or she did not have hospital cover; and (b) rounding up the result to
-- the nearest whole number."
@export How many years without hospital cover are counted against me (s 34-5(2))?
GIVEN `days counted` IS A NUMBER @desc Days without hospital cover that are not permitted days
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years without cover` IS
    IF TRUNC (`days counted` DIVIDED BY 365) 0 TIMES 365 LESS THAN `days counted`
    THEN TRUNC (`days counted` DIVIDED BY 365) 0 PLUS 1
    ELSE TRUNC (`days counted` DIVIDED BY 365) 0

§§ `ss 34-10, 37-15 -- the total loading, the 70% cap and the end after 10 years`

-- s 34-5(3): the s 34-5 increase is "in addition to any increase under section 34-1". s 37-15: "The maximum amount of any
-- increase under this Part ... is an amount equal to 70% of the base rate for the hospital cover."
-- s 34-10(1): the insurer "must stop increasing" premiums once the adult has had loaded hospital cover "(a) for a continuous period
-- of 10 years; or (b) for a period of 10 years that has been interrupted only by permitted days without hospital cover" (which do
-- not count towards the 10 years). s 34-10(2): it stops "on the day after the last day of the 10 year period". s 34-10(3): the
-- increase starts again if, after that, the adult drops cover, later takes it out again, and the days between "are not all
-- permitted days". INFERENCE: when it starts again, the same ss 34-1 and 34-5 percentages apply; the text does not say at what
-- level it resumes.
DECLARE `Loading facts` HAS
    `my date of birth` IS A NUMBER
    `day I took out hospital cover` IS A NUMBER
    `I had hospital cover on my base day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days without hospital cover that are not permitted days` IS A NUMBER
    `years of loaded cover counted towards the 10 years` IS A NUMBER
    `after the 10 years I dropped cover and the gap was not all permitted days` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `l` IS A `Loading facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the increase has stopped under s 34-10` MEANS
        `l`'s `years of loaded cover counted towards the 10 years` AT LEAST 10
    AND (NOT `l`'s `after the 10 years I dropped cover and the gap was not all permitted days`)

@export What is my total lifetime health cover loading, in percent of the base rate (ss 34-1, 34-5, 34-10, 37-15)?
GIVEN `l` IS A `Loading facts` @desc Your date of birth, when you took out cover, gaps in cover, and years of loaded cover held
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my lifetime health cover loading` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the increase has stopped under s 34-10` `l` THEN 0
        IF `l`'s `my date of birth` AT MOST 19340701 THEN 0
        OTHERWISE `the lesser of` 70 (`late` PLUS `dropped`)
    WHERE
        `late` MEANS `What is my late-joiner loading in percent` (`l`'s `my date of birth`) (`l`'s `day I took out hospital cover`)
                         (`l`'s `I had hospital cover on my base day`) (`l`'s `s 37-5 or s 37-10 treats me as having had cover`)
        `dropped` MEANS `How many years without cover` (`l`'s `days without hospital cover that are not permitted days`)
                            TIMES `the loading per year, in percent`

@export How much more do I pay a year for lifetime health cover, in dollars (ss 34-1, 37-15)?
GIVEN `base rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The premium for your hospital cover with no loading and no s 66-5(2) discount, in dollars a year
      `loading percent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifetime health cover loading, in percent of the base rate
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my loading in dollars` IS
    `base rate` TIMES (`the lesser of` 70 `loading percent`) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 37-20(2): for joint hospital cover, the increase is worked out "(a) dividing the base rate for the cover by the number of
-- adults it covers; and (b) using that rate to work out for each adult what the amount of the increase for that adult (if any)
-- would be; and (c) adding together the results". (Gloss: on a couple's policy, a loading on one partner applies to half the
-- premium.)
@export How much more do we pay a year on joint hospital cover for two adults, in dollars (s 37-20)?
GIVEN `base rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The premium for the joint hospital cover with no loading, in dollars a year
      `my loading percent` IS A NUMBER @desc Your lifetime health cover loading, in percent
      `the other adult's loading percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The other adult's lifetime health cover loading, in percent
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is our joint loading in dollars` IS
      `How much is my loading in dollars` (`base rate` DIVIDED BY 2) `my loading percent`
    PLUS `How much is my loading in dollars` (`base rate` DIVIDED BY 2) `the other adult's loading percent`

§§ `ss 22-30, 22-35, 22-40 -- private health insurance tiers`

-- s 22-30(1): the families table applies if "(a) on the last day of the financial year, the person is married" or "(b) on any
-- day in the financial year, the person contributes in a substantial way to the maintenance of a dependent person who is" the
-- person's child or sibling. s 22-30(2): the spouse's "income for surcharge purposes ... [is] included in the first person's".
-- s 22-30(4): otherwise the singles table. Each table: "tier 1 earner" above the tier 1 threshold and not above tier 2; "tier 2
-- earner" above tier 2 and not above tier 3; "tier 3 earner" above tier 3.
-- s 22-35: singles thresholds "$90,000", "$105,000", "$140,000" "for the 2021-22 and 2022-23 financial year", indexed under
-- s 22-45 (rounded down to $1,000; never lowered: s 22-45(3), (3A)). The indexed figures are not deposited: INPUTS.
-- s 22-40(1)-(3): each family threshold is "double" the singles one; s 22-40(4): increased for 2 or more dependent children by a
-- formula the deposit drops: an INPUT. Same tier names as the Medicare Levy Act baseline (whose s 3A replaces s 22-30(1)(b)).
DECLARE Tier IS ONE OF
    `not above the tier 1 threshold`
    `a tier 1 earner`
    `a tier 2 earner`
    `a tier 3 earner`

DECLARE `Tier facts` HAS
    `I am married on the last day of the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I maintain a dependent child or sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `my spouse's income for surcharge purposes` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 1 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 2 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `my singles tier 3 threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children` IS A NUMBER

@export Does the families table of private health insurance tiers apply to me (s 22-30(1))?
GIVEN `t` IS A `Tier facts` @desc Your marriage, dependants, income for surcharge purposes and the year's thresholds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the families table apply to me` IF
    `t`'s `I am married on the last day of the financial year` OR `t`'s `I maintain a dependent child or sibling`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Tier facts`, `singles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my threshold from` MEANS
    IF `Does the families table apply to me` `t`
    THEN 2 TIMES `singles` PLUS `t`'s `increase in my family thresholds for two or more children`
    ELSE `singles`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Tier facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my income for the tiers` MEANS
    IF `t`'s `I am married on the last day of the financial year`
    THEN `t`'s `my income for surcharge purposes` PLUS `t`'s `my spouse's income for surcharge purposes`
    ELSE `t`'s `my income for surcharge purposes`

@export Which private health insurance income tier am I in (s 22-30)?
GIVEN `t` IS A `Tier facts` @desc Your marriage, dependants, income for surcharge purposes and the year's thresholds
GIVETH A Tier
DECIDE `Which income tier am I in` IS
    IF `my income for the tiers` `t` GREATER THAN `my threshold from` `t` (`t`'s `my singles tier 3 threshold`) THEN `a tier 3 earner`
    ELSE IF `my income for the tiers` `t` GREATER THAN `my threshold from` `t` (`t`'s `my singles tier 2 threshold`) THEN `a tier 2 earner`
         ELSE IF `my income for the tiers` `t` GREATER THAN `my threshold from` `t` (`t`'s `my singles tier 1 threshold`) THEN `a tier 1 earner`
              ELSE `not above the tier 1 threshold`

§§ `ss 22-15, 22-20 -- my share of the rebate (the PHII benefit)`

-- s 22-15(1): the share is "(a) 30% of the amount of the premium ... in respect of days ... on which no person insured under the
-- policy was aged 65 years or over"; "(b) 35%" where someone insured is 65 to 69; "(c) 40%" where someone insured is 70 or over.
-- s 22-15(2), (3): "Reduce ... by 10 percentage points" for a tier 1 earner, "by 20 percentage points" for a tier 2 earner;
-- s 22-15(4): "to nil" for a tier 3 earner. s 22-15(5A)-(5E): each percentage in (1), (2) and (3) is multiplied each 1 April
-- (from 2014) by an adjustment factor set by the Incentives Rules (never more than 1) -- not deposited, so the adjusted
-- percentages are INPUTS; the Act's own figures are given by `the percentages as the Act states them`.
DECLARE `Oldest person insured` IS ONE OF
    `everyone insured under 65`
    `someone insured 65 to 69`
    `someone insured 70 or over`

DECLARE `Rebate percentages` HAS
    `under 65` IS A NUMBER
    `65 to 69` IS A NUMBER
    `70 or over` IS A NUMBER
    `tier 1 reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `tier 2 reduction` IS A NUMBER

DECIDE `the percentages as the Act states them` IS `Rebate percentages` WITH
    `under 65` IS 30
    `65 to 69` IS 35
    `70 or over` IS 40
    `tier 1 reduction` IS 10
    `tier 2 reduction` IS 20

@export What percentage of my premium is my private health insurance rebate (s 22-15)?
GIVEN `oldest` IS AN `Oldest person insured` @desc The age of the oldest person insured under the policy on the days in question
      `tier` IS A Tier @desc Your private health insurance income tier for the financial year
      `percentages` IS A `Rebate percentages` @desc The s 22-15 percentages as adjusted under s 22-15(5A) for the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my rebate percentage` IS
    CONSIDER `tier`
    WHEN `a tier 3 earner` THEN 0
    WHEN `a tier 2 earner` THEN `the base percentage` MINUS `percentages`'s `tier 2 reduction`
    WHEN `a tier 1 earner` THEN `the base percentage` MINUS `percentages`'s `tier 1 reduction`
    OTHERWISE `the base percentage`
    WHERE
        `the base percentage` MEANS
            CONSIDER `oldest`
            WHEN `someone insured 70 or over` THEN `percentages`'s `70 or over`
            WHEN `someone insured 65 to 69` THEN `percentages`'s `65 to 69`
            OTHERWISE `percentages`'s `under 65`

-- s 22-15(6): the percentages apply to the premium reduced "by any part of that amount that is attributable to an increase in
-- the premium in accordance with Division 34". (Gloss: no rebate on the lifetime health cover loading.) s 22-20: with more than
-- one PHIIB, each share is worked out as if "the premium ... divided by the number of persons who are PHIIBs". s 22-5(1): each
-- adult insured throughout the premium period is a PHIIB ("private health insurance incentive beneficiary").
@export How much is my share of the private health insurance rebate on a premium, in dollars (ss 22-15, 22-20)?
GIVEN `premium` IS A NUMBER @desc The premium paid or payable, in dollars
      `of it, lifetime health cover loading` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the premium that is lifetime health cover loading, in dollars
      `number of PHIIBs` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of adults insured under the policy throughout the premium period
      `my rebate percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc Your rebate percentage under s 22-15
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my share of the rebate` IS
    (`premium` MINUS `of it, lifetime health cover loading`) DIVIDED BY `number of PHIIBs` TIMES `my rebate percentage` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `ss 55-5, 55-10, 55-15 -- community rating`

-- s 55-5(1): "A private health insurer must not ... take or fail to take any action; or ... have regard or fail to have regard
-- to any matter; that would result in the insurer improperly discriminating between people who are or wish to be insured".
-- s 55-5(2): improper discrimination relates to "(a) ... a chronic disease, illness or other medical condition"; "(b) the gender,
-- race, sexual orientation or religious belief"; "(c) the age of a person, except to the extent allowed under ... Part 2-3
-- (lifetime health cover)" or an allowed age-based discount; "(d) where a person lives, except to the extent allowed" for
-- approved regional premiums; "(e) any other characteristic ... (including ... occupation or leisure pursuits) that is likely to
-- result in an increased need for hospital treatment or general treatment"; "(f) the frequency with which a person needs"
-- treatment; "(g) the amount or extent of the benefits" claimed, except under s 66-15. s 55-5(3): a restricted access insurer
-- may keep its products to the people its rules allow. s 55-5(4), (5): an employer-group discount meeting s 66-5 is allowed,
-- but not cancelling the policy because employment ends. s 55-10: closing or terminating a product; s 55-15: pilot projects.
DECLARE `What the insurer acts on` IS ONE OF
    `my medical condition or illness`
    `my gender, race, sexual orientation or religious belief`
    `my age, beyond lifetime health cover and allowed discounts`
    `my lifetime health cover loading`
    `where I live, beyond an approved regional premium`
    `my occupation or leisure pursuits that raise my need for treatment`
    `how often I need treatment`
    `how much I have claimed, beyond s 66-15`
    `my not being eligible under a restricted access insurer's rules`
    `an employer-group discount that meets s 66-5`
    `my employment ending, by cancelling my policy`
    `the insurer closing or terminating the product`
    `a pilot project under the Complying Product Rules`

@export May my insurer refuse to insure me, or treat me differently, because of this (ss 55-5, 55-10, 55-15)?
GIVEN `reason` IS A `What the insurer acts on` @desc What the insurer is acting on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my insurer act on this` IF
    CONSIDER `reason`
    WHEN `my lifetime health cover loading` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my not being eligible under a restricted access insurer's rules` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employer-group discount that meets s 66-5` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the insurer closing or terminating the product` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a pilot project under the Complying Product Rules` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 102-1 -- hospital cover must be on offer`

-- s 102-1: "At any time when a private health insurer makes available a complying health insurance product that covers general
-- treatment, the insurer must also make available a complying health insurance product that covers hospital treatment."
@export Must an insurer that sells me general (extras) cover also offer hospital cover (s 102-1)?
GIVEN `the insurer offers a complying product covering general treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer makes available a complying product that covers general (extras) treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the insurer offer hospital cover` IF
    `the insurer offers a complying product covering general treatment`
